  "answer_text": "It's currently the **2026 NBA Finals**, with the New York Knicks facing the San Antonio Spurs! Here are the best places to get tickets:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfc0 Where to Buy NBA Finals Tickets\n\n1. **Ticketmaster** *(Official Ticketing Partner of the NBA)*\n- NBA tickets for the 2025\u20132026 season are available to purchase on Ticketmaster, the Official Ticketing Partner of the NBA, where you can browse a wide selection of tickets.\n- If tickets for a game are sold out, additional seats may become available closer to the game, so keep checking back.\n- Visit: [ticketmaster.com/nba](https://www.ticketmaster.com/nba)\n\n2. **NBA.com**\n- The official NBA website has a schedule and ticketing section where you can find upcoming games and links to purchase tickets.\n- Visit: [nba.com/schedule](https://www.nba.com/schedule)\n\n3. **ESPN**\n- The complete 2026 NBA season schedule on ESPN includes game times, TV listings, and ticket information for all NBA games.\n- Visit: [espn.com/nba/schedule](https://www.espn.com/nba/schedule)\n\n4. **Third-Party Ticket Sites**\n- Sites like [nbatickets.us](https://nbatickets.us/) and [americanarenas.com](https://americanarenas.com/tickets/nba-finals/) also list available tickets, including VIP packages.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcb0 Current NBA Finals Ticket Prices\nNBA Finals tickets for 2026 start at $1,009. Ticket prices and availability update frequently, so it's best to check early and often.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfc6 Current Series Status\nThe Knicks held off a late rally from the Spurs in Game 2 to take a 2-0 lead in the 2026 NBA Finals. Games 3 and beyond are still up for grabs!\n\nWould you like help finding tickets for a specific game or city?",
